From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 21:32:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 086/190] segacd: the cache cannot be larger than the chip's
 buffer

Pooled hardware failures -- 1608, 1617, 1618, 1620 -- land late in a
read run and never early: 1608 ends a FAT walk that began at 1600,
the others follow a root scan that began at 1616. Position within the
run, not position on the disc.

Twelve per fill was set on the reasoning that one seek should serve a
whole structure. The reasoning was right and the number was not: the
decoder's RAM is 16 KB and a block is 2352 bytes, so it holds 6.9,
and the recycler was measured arriving at five. The last five sectors
of every twelve were overwritten before the read reached them.

Six is what one streaming pass can actually carry.
---
 bios/segacd.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bios/segacd.c b/bios/segacd.c
index 036e3e0..25b093c 100644
--- a/bios/segacd.c
+++ b/bios/segacd.c
@@ -2106,7 +2106,7 @@ static void cd_park(void)
  * milliseconds apart and free -- Lunar drains everything available
  * before it yields, for this reason -- so the only cost of taking
  * twelve is the buffer. */
-#define CD_CACHE_SECTORS 12
+#define CD_CACHE_SECTORS 6
 
 static UBYTE cd_cache[CD_CACHE_SECTORS][CDC_DATA_BYTES];
 
